Planetary theory VSOP87 (generated: internal/ephemeris/vsop87_earth.go and
planet/vsop87_*.go)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The heliocentric positions of the Earth, from which the Sun's position follows,
and of the other seven planets are the VSOP87D solution of Bretagnon and
Francou, truncated by amplitude. The tables are generated by
internal/cmd/genvsop from the files distributed by the Institut de mécanique
céleste et de calcul des éphémérides (IMCCE); each generated header records the
source file and its SHA-256.

  Bretagnon, P., Francou, G. 1988, "Planetary theories in rectangular and
    spherical variables. VSOP87 solutions", Astronomy and Astrophysics, 202, 309.
  https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/planets/vsop87/

The planet package also uses the IAU planetary radii and Uranus's pole from the
report of the IAU Working Group on Cartographic Coordinates and Rotational
Elements, and the apparent magnitude formulas of Mallama and Hilton:

  Archinal, B. A., et al. 2018, "Report of the IAU Working Group on Cartographic
    Coordinates and Rotational Elements: 2015", Celestial Mechanics and
    Dynamical Astronomy, 130, 22.
  Mallama, A., Hilton, J. L. 2018, "Computing apparent planetary magnitudes for
    The Astronomical Almanac", Astronomy and Computing, 25, 10.

