Lunar theory ELP 2000-82B (generated: internal/elp/table.go)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Moon's geocentric position is the ELP 2000-82B lunar solution of
Chapront-Touze and Chapront, with its constants fitted to JPL's DE200/LE200,
truncated by amplitude. The table is generated by internal/cmd/genelp from the
36 files and the Fortran subroutine ELP82B_2 distributed by the Institut de
mécanique céleste et de calcul des éphémérides (IMCCE); the generator pins each
file's SHA-256.

  Chapront-Touze, M., Chapront, J. 1983, "The lunar ephemeris ELP 2000",
    Astronomy and Astrophysics, 124, 50.
  Chapront-Touze, M., Chapront, J. 1988, "ELP 2000-85: a semi-analytical lunar
    ephemeris adequate for historical times", Astronomy and Astrophysics, 190,
    342.
  https://ftp.imcce.fr/pub/ephem/moon/elp82b/

