SGP4/SDP4 satellite propagation (satellite/sgp4.go)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The satellite propagator is a port of the reference implementation published
with Vallado, Crawford, Hujsak and Kelso (2006), which its authors released to
the public domain, made by way of its Python transliteration in python-sgp4.
The verification set in satellite/testdata (SGP4-VER.TLE, tcppver.out) is the
one distributed with that reference code. The sample OMM messages are the ones
python-sgp4 ships.

  Vallado, D. A., Crawford, P., Hujsak, R., Kelso, T. S. 2006, "Revisiting
    Spacetrack Report #3", AIAA 2006-6753.
  python-sgp4, Copyright (c) 2012-2016 Brandon Rhodes
  https://github.com/brandon-rhodes/python-sgp4
  License: MIT

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Elevation data (fetched at run time by the optional openmeteo package)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The openmeteo package asks the Open-Meteo elevation API for an observer's
height. No elevation data is embedded. Open-Meteo serves the Copernicus DEM
GLO-90; its data is offered under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 licence,
and a consumer that shows the heights should credit Open-Meteo.

  https://open-meteo.com/en/docs/elevation-api

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Star catalog (embedded: star/data/stars.csv)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The embedded star catalog is a curated subset of the HYG database
(Hipparcos-Yale-Gliese), compiled by David Nash / Astronomy Nexus. The subset
contains stars with apparent magnitude <= 6.5 together with every star carrying
a proper name; the remaining rows and columns of the full ~120,000-star catalog
are omitted to keep the binary small.

  HYG database, version 4.4
  https://codeberg.org/astronexus/hyg
  License: Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0)
  https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

The star catalog data in star/data/stars.csv remains licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Constellation boundaries (embedded: constellation/data/boundaries.csv)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The constellation boundary table is the official IAU constellation boundaries
established by Eugène Delporte (1930) and rearranged for position lookup by
Nancy G. Roman (1987), distributed as VizieR catalog VI/42.

  Delporte, E. 1930, "Delimitation Scientifique des Constellations",
    Cambridge University Press.
  Roman, N. G. 1987, "Identification of a Constellation from a Position",
    Publications of the Astronomical Society of the Pacific, 99, 695.
  VizieR VI/42: https://vizier.cds.unistra.fr/viz-bin/VizieR?-source=VI/42
